A||||9||Mach10||Slightly worrisome problem||||8||
Z||000000||Mach10||06-24-2001||05:40 PM||||Driving to the store to get parts, I noticed that my temp gage was climbing high. I ignored it, since traffic was slow, but 5 minutes later, it hit red, and the light came on. I immediately hit the turnsignal, and started to pull off the road, when suddenly, the gage twitched, and started to fall rapidly. I thought, "well what the hell?!?" and kept going. When I pull up to a stop, the gage climbs slowly, to 3/4 up, and when I start moving, it drops quickly. <BR>WHAT THE HELL IS GOING ON?!?<BR>The heater vents blow hot air continuously, so it doesn't seem to be a circulation problem, at least from the water pump, and the system was flushed last month. The engine isn't behaving like it's overheating, but I'm not taking chances... WTF is going on?!?||||reg||8
Z||000001||DecadenceR||06-24-2001||05:53 PM||||That sounds like the problem I had when my fan stopped working.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||06-24-2001||06:00 PM||||Oh, **** .||||reg||8
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-24-2001||06:04 PM||||check the water again.. sounds like its getting airlocked.<P>also could be your thermostat sticking.  you might try to remove it since you wont need it before winter anyways..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||06-24-2001||06:05 PM||||If you have AC, turn it on when the temp goes up, that should turn on the fan.  If it doesn't: fan switch, fan motor bad||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||06-24-2001||06:31 PM||||Before now, the water system was in great shape. I'm not so sure that the system's airlocked, as the heater will blow HOT air at all times, which suggests good circulation when the engine is running. <BR>Also, the temperature climbs slowly, but falls rapidly. That's not consistent with my experience in cooling systems, which tend towards the reverse (i.e., heats up FAST and cools slow) I'm fairly sure the fan's working. I'm wondering if the temperature sensor is buggered?||||reg||13
Z||000006||rogergarrison||06-24-2001||08:36 PM||||sounds to me like a sticking thermostat too.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||06-24-2001||08:41 PM||||I just changed the Tstat for a 160*, and the problem isn't coming back at idle. I hope that fixed it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>Big scare  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000008||Mach10||06-25-2001||03:36 AM||||As I sit here, mildly wasted, I reflect that yeah, it *was* the thermostat. No problems since. Thanks for the help guys! I'll drink another for you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000009||84Bill||06-25-2001||09:23 AM||||Just a heads up on this issue, My temp gauge acts very erraticly untill the engine is actually warmed up. I don't know weather it's the temp sender or the guage. Either way I ignore the temp for about the first 15 minutes after startup||||reg||1
